  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STRENGTHENING CONSERVATION OF THE ENDANGERED PILEATED GIBBON (HYLOBATES PILEATUS) IN PREY LANG WILDLIFE SANCTUARY, CAMBODIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO IMPROVE THE CONSERVATION STATUS OF ENDANGERED PILEATED GIBBONS AND THEIR HABITATS IN PREY LANG WILDLIFE SANCTUARY (PLWS) THROUGH TARGETED MONITORING AND BY ENGAGING LOCAL STAKEHOLDERS, PRIMARILY INDIGENOUS KUY PEOPLE, IN THEIR PROTECTION. PROJECT OBJECTIVES ARE (1) A MONITORING PROGRAM IS ESTABLISHED FOR ASSESSING TRENDS IN POPULATION ABUNDANCE AND DISTRIBUTION OF PILEATED GIBBONS IN PLWS AND (2) REDUCED THREATS TO GIBBONS AND THEIR HABITATS THROUGH EFFECTIVE CO-MANAGEMENT WITH LOCAL COMMUNITIES AND PROTECTED AREA RANGERS.</narrative>
  </description>
